## Context
Exposed by the fifth smelt (PR #2049): git page open questions
(`memory/topics/git-worktree-session-guards.md`); the ruling is pinned on the
Commission page. Filed under SMELT.md v8-r5.

Claim A, author ruling 2026-10-30 ("KISS on 1366"): PR 2035 kept the
commit-id push and dropped the ls-remote read-back
(`memory/journal/2026/2026-10-30-rulings-and-memory-design-input.md`). The
gate flagged the departure; "The author merged anyway and declined to narrow
the rule: the distinction below is memory, not rule"
(`memory/journal/2026/2026-10-30-push-by-commit-id-exit-code-1366.md`). The
distinction: a push by commit id lands or is refused, so its exit code answers.

Claim B, `rules/git.md` § Reading state: "Verify a forge mutation by reading it
back, in the same command. Exit codes and warnings do not tell you whether it
landed."

## Question for the author
Does a push by commit id count as verified by its exit code, against the
written rule? If yes, does the exception stay in memory (jurisprudence) or
reach the rule? Smelt picks no side.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The author's answer is recorded here
- [ ] Memory pages and the rule agree, or the page keeps the conflict open by the author's choice
